{"context": "published", "host": "www.josephsmithpapers.org", "showHeader": true, "footerStyle": "mini", "statusCode": 200, "uri": "letter-to-edward-partridge-and-others-10-december-1833", "page": "2", "is404": false, "gallery": [{"image": "/7633/7633_ms155_2_01_lb1_070_thumb.jpg", "page": "1", "label": "70", "href": "/paper-summary/letter-to-edward-partridge-and-others-10-december-1833/1"}, {"image": "/7633/7633_ms155_2_01_lb1_071_thumb.jpg", "page": "2", "label": "71", "href": "/paper-summary/letter-to-edward-partridge-and-others-10-december-1833/2"}, {"image": "/7633/7633_ms155_2_01_lb1_072_thumb.jpg", "page": "3", "label": "72", "href": "/paper-summary/letter-to-edward-partridge-and-others-10-december-1833/3"}, {"image": "/7633/7633_ms155_2_01_lb1_073_thumb.jpg", "page": "4", "label": "73", "href": "/paper-summary/letter-to-edward-partridge-and-others-10-december-1833/4"}, {"image": "/7633/7633_ms155_2_01_lb1_074_thumb.jpg", "page": "5", "label": "74", "href": "/paper-summary/letter-to-edward-partridge-and-others-10-december-1833/5"}, {"image": "/7633/7633_ms155_2_01_lb1_075_thumb.jpg", "page": "6", "label": "75", "href": "/paper-summary/letter-to-edward-partridge-and-others-10-december-1833/6"}], "tableOfContents": [], "summary": {"uri": "letter-to-edward-partridge-and-others-10-december-1833", "series": "JSPPD", "urlTitleValue": "JSPPD3", "documentSeriesTitle": "Letter to Edward Partridge and Others, 10 December 1833", "editorialPageNumber": "71", "isPageNumberPresent": true, "searchUrl": "/published/jsp/searchable/papers/30495/30495-0002.xml", "clearText": "<html><head></head><body><div class=\"indent continuation wasptag\"> with their blood.<aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"16605417159715401625\"><a href=\"#16605417159715401625\" class=\"editorial-note-static staticPopup\" title=\"Note\" name=\"trans4\"><span id=\"documenttrans4\">4</span></a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data editorial-footnote\" isnote=\"Y\"><p class=\"bottom_0\">See Ezekiel 20:40; and Isaiah 57:13; see also <a href=\"/paper-summary/revelation-22-23-september-1832-dc-84\" class=\"referenceInPop\" pop=\"/ajax/papers/tooltip/revelation-22-23-september-1832-dc-84\" poptitle=\"Revelation, 22–23 September 1832\n[D&amp;C 84]\">Revelation, 22–23 Sept. 1832</a> [D&amp;C 84:2].</p><hr></div></div></aside> I cannot learn from any communication by the spirit to me that <aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"5966516138774921395\"><a href=\"#5966516138774921395\" class=\"reference staticPopup\" ro=\"x4116\" topic=\"x4116\" title=\"Zion\">Zion</a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data\" isnote=\"Y\" isnonsearchable=\"Y\"><input type=\"hidden\" value=\"Zion\"><p>A specific location in Missouri; also a literal or figurative gathering of believers in Jesus Christ, characterized by adherence to ideals of harmony, equality, and purity. In JS’s earliest revelations “the cause of Zion” was used to broadly describe the ...</p><a class=\"more\" href=\"/topic/zion\">View Glossary</a></div></div></aside> has forfeited her claim to a celestial crown notwithstanding the Lord has caused her to be thus afflicted; except it may be some individuals who have walked in disobedience and forsaken the <aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"16505324299603777532\"><a href=\"#16505324299603777532\" class=\"reference staticPopup\" ro=\"x4095\" topic=\"x4095\" title=\"Everlasting covenant\">new covenants</a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data\" isnote=\"Y\" isnonsearchable=\"Y\"><input type=\"hidden\" value=\"Everlasting covenant\"><p>Generally referred to the “fulness of the gospel”—the sum total of the church’s message, geared toward establishing God’s covenant people on the earth; also used to describe individual elements of the gospel, including marriage. According to JS, the everlasting...</p><a class=\"more\" href=\"/topic/everlasting-covenant\">View Glossary</a></div></div></aside>; all such will be made manifest by their works in due time. I have always expected that Zion would suffer sore affliction from what I could learn from the commandments which have been given.<aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"3572593500961286307\"><a href=\"#3572593500961286307\" class=\"editorial-note-static staticPopup\" title=\"Note\" name=\"trans5\"><span id=\"documenttrans5\">5</span></a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data editorial-footnote\" isnote=\"Y\"><p class=\"bottom_0\">Four months earlier, on 2 August 1833, JS dictated a <a href=\"/paper-summary/revelation-2-august-1833-a-dc-97\" class=\"referenceInPop\" pop=\"/ajax/papers/tooltip/revelation-2-august-1833-a-dc-97\" poptitle=\"Revelation,\n2 August 1833–A [D&amp;C\n97]\">revelation</a> that warned if <a href=\"/topic/zion\" class=\"referenceInPop\">Zion</a> “observe not to do whatsoeve[r] I have <a href=\"/topic/commandment\" class=\"referenceInPop\">commanded</a> her I will visit her according to all her works with sore afflictions.” (<a href=\"/paper-summary/revelation-2-august-1833-a-dc-97\" class=\"referenceInPop\" pop=\"/ajax/papers/tooltip/revelation-2-august-1833-a-dc-97\" poptitle=\"Revelation,\n2 August 1833–A [D&amp;C\n97]\">Revelation, 2 Aug. 1833–A</a> [D&amp;C 97:26].)</p><hr></div></div></aside> but I would remind you of a certain clause in one which says that after <span class=\"underscore\">much</span> tribulation cometh the <span class=\"underscore\">blessing</span>.<aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"12526569500028809258\"><a href=\"#12526569500028809258\" class=\"editorial-note-static staticPopup\" title=\"Note\" name=\"trans6\"><span id=\"documenttrans6\">6</span></a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data editorial-footnote\" isnote=\"Y\"><p class=\"bottom_0\">See <a href=\"/paper-summary/revelation-1-august-1831-dc-58\" class=\"referenceInPop\" pop=\"/ajax/papers/tooltip/revelation-1-august-1831-dc-58\" poptitle=\"Revelation, 1 August 1831 [D&amp;C\n58]\">Revelation, 1 Aug. 1831</a> [D&amp;C 58:4].</p><hr></div></div></aside> by this and also others, and also one received of late, I know that Zion, in the own due time of the Lord will be redeemed,<aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"3430351123795326722\"><a href=\"#3430351123795326722\" class=\"editorial-note-static staticPopup\" title=\"Note\" name=\"trans7\"><span id=\"documenttrans7\">7</span></a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data editorial-footnote\" isnote=\"Y\"><p class=\"bottom_0\">See <a href=\"/paper-summary/revelation-12-october-1833-dc-100\" class=\"referenceInPop\" pop=\"/ajax/papers/tooltip/revelation-12-october-1833-dc-100\" poptitle=\"Revelation, 12\nOctober 1833 [D&amp;C 100]\">Revelation, 12 Oct. 1833</a> [D&amp;C 100:13].</p><hr></div></div></aside> but how many will be the days of her purification, tribulation and affliction, the Lord has kept hid from my eyes; and when I enquire concerning this subject the voice of the Lord is, Be still, and know that I am God!<aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"7051714876851975379\"><a href=\"#7051714876851975379\" class=\"editorial-note-static staticPopup\" title=\"Note\" name=\"trans8\"><span id=\"documenttrans8\">8</span></a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data editorial-footnote\" isnote=\"Y\"><p class=\"bottom_0\">See Psalm 46:10. Six days after he wrote this letter, JS dictated a <a href=\"/paper-summary/revelation-16-17-december-1833-dc-101\" class=\"referenceInPop\" pop=\"/ajax/papers/tooltip/revelation-16-17-december-1833-dc-101\" poptitle=\"Revelation, 16–17 December 1833 [D&amp;C\n101]\">revelation</a> reiterating this sentiment. (<a href=\"/paper-summary/revelation-16-17-december-1833-dc-101\" class=\"referenceInPop\" pop=\"/ajax/papers/tooltip/revelation-16-17-december-1833-dc-101\" poptitle=\"Revelation, 16–17 December 1833 [D&amp;C\n101]\">Revelation, 16–17 Dec. 1833</a> [D&amp;C 101:16].)</p><hr></div></div></aside> all those who suffer for my name shall reign with me,<aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"15407606302483454135\"><a href=\"#15407606302483454135\" class=\"editorial-note-static staticPopup\" title=\"Note\" name=\"trans9\"><span id=\"documenttrans9\">9</span></a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data editorial-footnote\" isnote=\"Y\"><p class=\"bottom_0\">See 2 Timothy 2:12.</p><hr></div></div></aside> and he that layeth down his life for my sake shall find it again.<aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"12561625369031436329\"><a href=\"#12561625369031436329\" class=\"editorial-note-static staticPopup\" title=\"Note\" name=\"trans10\"><span id=\"documenttrans10\">10</span></a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data editorial-footnote\" isnote=\"Y\"><p class=\"bottom_0\">See Luke 9:24; and <a href=\"/paper-summary/revelation-6-august-1833-dc-98\" class=\"referenceInPop\" pop=\"/ajax/papers/tooltip/revelation-6-august-1833-dc-98\" poptitle=\"Revelation,\n6 August 1833 [D&amp;C\n98]\">Revelation, 6 Aug. 1833</a> [D&amp;C 98:13].</p><hr></div></div></aside> Now there are two things of which I am ignorant and the Lord will not show me— perhaps for a wise purpose in himself. I mean in some respects, and they are these, Why God hath suffered so great calamity to come upon Zion; or what the great moving cause of this great affliction is.<aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"5736489044884305988\"><a href=\"#5736489044884305988\" class=\"editorial-note-static staticPopup\" title=\"Note\" name=\"trans11\"><span id=\"documenttrans11\">11</span></a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data editorial-footnote\" isnote=\"Y\"><p class=\"bottom_0\">JS dictated a <a href=\"/paper-summary/revelation-16-17-december-1833-dc-101\" class=\"referenceInPop\" pop=\"/ajax/papers/tooltip/revelation-16-17-december-1833-dc-101\" poptitle=\"Revelation, 16–17 December 1833 [D&amp;C\n101]\">revelation</a> about a week later that read, “There were jar[r]ings and contentions envyings and strifes and lustful and covetous desires among them . . . they were slow to hearken unto the voice of the Lord their God Therefore the Lord their God is slow to hearken unto their prayers to answer them in the day of their trouble In the day of their peace they esteemed lightly my council.” (<a href=\"/paper-summary/revelation-16-17-december-1833-dc-101\" class=\"referenceInPop\" pop=\"/ajax/papers/tooltip/revelation-16-17-december-1833-dc-101\" poptitle=\"Revelation, 16–17 December 1833 [D&amp;C\n101]\">Revelation, 16–17 Dec. 1833</a> [D&amp;C 101:6–8].)</p><hr></div></div></aside> and again by what means he will return her back to her <aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"11819206501905069875\"><a href=\"#11819206501905069875\" class=\"reference staticPopup\" ro=\"x6228\" topic=\"x6228\" title=\"Inheritance\">inheritance</a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data\" isnote=\"Y\" isnonsearchable=\"Y\"><input type=\"hidden\" value=\"Inheritance\"><p>Generally referred to land promised by or received from God for the church and its members. A January 1831 revelation promised church members a land of inheritance. In March and May 1831, JS dictated revelations commanding members “to purchase lands for an...</p><a class=\"more\" href=\"/topic/inheritance\">View Glossary</a></div></div></aside> with songs of everlasting Joy upon her head.<aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"7846441802007527689\"><a href=\"#7846441802007527689\" class=\"editorial-note-static staticPopup\" title=\"Note\" name=\"trans12\"><span id=\"documenttrans12\">12</span></a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data editorial-footnote\" isnote=\"Y\"><p class=\"bottom_0\">See Isaiah 35:10; 51:11; <a href=\"/paper-summary/revelation-circa-7-march-1831-dc-45\" class=\"referenceInPop\" pop=\"/ajax/papers/tooltip/revelation-circa-7-march-1831-dc-45\" poptitle=\"Revelation, circa 7 March 1831 [D&amp;C\n45]\">Revelation, ca. 7 Mar. 1831</a> [D&amp;C 45:71]; and <a href=\"/paper-summary/revelation-29-october-1831-dc-66\" class=\"referenceInPop\" pop=\"/ajax/papers/tooltip/revelation-29-october-1831-dc-66\" poptitle=\"Revelation, 29\nOctober 1831 [D&amp;C 66]\">Revelation, 29 Oct. 1831</a> [D&amp;C 66:11].</p><hr></div></div></aside> These two things brethren, are in part kept back that they are not plainly shewn unto me. but there are some things that are plainly manifest, that has incured the displeasure of the Almighty. when I contemplate upon all things that have been [p. 71]</div></body></html>", "expandedText": "<html><head></head><body><div class=\"indent continuation wasptag\"> with their blood.<aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"244866308034964329\"><a href=\"#244866308034964329\" class=\"editorial-note-static staticPopup\" title=\"Note\" name=\"trans4\"><span id=\"documenttrans4\">4</span></a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data editorial-footnote\" isnote=\"Y\"><p class=\"bottom_0\">See Ezekiel 20:40; and Isaiah 57:13; see also <a href=\"/paper-summary/revelation-22-23-september-1832-dc-84\" class=\"referenceInPop\" pop=\"/ajax/papers/tooltip/revelation-22-23-september-1832-dc-84\" poptitle=\"Revelation, 22–23 September 1832\n[D&amp;C 84]\">Revelation, 22–23 Sept. 1832</a> [D&amp;C 84:2].</p><hr></div></div></aside> I cannot learn from any com<span class=\"line-break hyphenate\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>munication by the spirit to me that <aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"10615759793519283362\"><a href=\"#10615759793519283362\" class=\"reference staticPopup\" ro=\"x4116\" topic=\"x4116\" title=\"Zion\">Zion</a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data\" isnote=\"Y\" isnonsearchable=\"Y\"><input type=\"hidden\" value=\"Zion\"><p>A specific location in Missouri; also a literal or figurative gathering of believers in Jesus Christ, characterized by adherence to ideals of harmony, equality, and purity. In JS’s earliest revelations “the cause of Zion” was used to broadly describe the ...</p><a class=\"more\" href=\"/topic/zion\">View Glossary</a></div></div></aside> has <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>forfeited her claim to a celestial crown not<span class=\"line-break hyphenate\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>withstanding the Lord has caused her to be <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>thus afflicted; except it may <span class=\"deleted\">it may</span> be some <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>individuals who have walked in disobedience <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>and forsaken the <aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"14197881510284072596\"><a href=\"#14197881510284072596\" class=\"reference staticPopup\" ro=\"x4095\" topic=\"x4095\" title=\"Everlasting covenant\">new covenants</a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data\" isnote=\"Y\" isnonsearchable=\"Y\"><input type=\"hidden\" value=\"Everlasting covenant\"><p>Generally referred to the “fulness of the gospel”—the sum total of the church’s message, geared toward establishing God’s covenant people on the earth; also used to describe individual elements of the gospel, including marriage. According to JS, the everlasting...</p><a class=\"more\" href=\"/topic/everlasting-covenant\">View Glossary</a></div></div></aside>; all such will <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>be made manifest by their works in due time. <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>I have always expected that Zion would suffer sore <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>affliction from what I could learn from the com<span class=\"line-break hyphenate\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>mandments which have been given.<aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"4040432009142619244\"><a href=\"#4040432009142619244\" class=\"editorial-note-static staticPopup\" title=\"Note\" name=\"trans5\"><span id=\"documenttrans5\">5</span></a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data editorial-footnote\" isnote=\"Y\"><p class=\"bottom_0\">Four months earlier, on 2 August 1833, JS dictated a <a href=\"/paper-summary/revelation-2-august-1833-a-dc-97\" class=\"referenceInPop\" pop=\"/ajax/papers/tooltip/revelation-2-august-1833-a-dc-97\" poptitle=\"Revelation,\n2 August 1833–A [D&amp;C\n97]\">revelation</a> that warned if <a href=\"/topic/zion\" class=\"referenceInPop\">Zion</a> “observe not to do whatsoeve[r] I have <a href=\"/topic/commandment\" class=\"referenceInPop\">commanded</a> her I will visit her according to all her works with sore afflictions.” (<a href=\"/paper-summary/revelation-2-august-1833-a-dc-97\" class=\"referenceInPop\" pop=\"/ajax/papers/tooltip/revelation-2-august-1833-a-dc-97\" poptitle=\"Revelation,\n2 August 1833–A [D&amp;C\n97]\">Revelation, 2 Aug. 1833–A</a> [D&amp;C 97:26].)</p><hr></div></div></aside> but I would <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>remind you of a certain clause in one which says <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>that after <span class=\"underscore\">much</span> tribulation cometh the <span class=\"underscore\">blessing</span>.<aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"10413754604294689899\"><a href=\"#10413754604294689899\" class=\"editorial-note-static staticPopup\" title=\"Note\" name=\"trans6\"><span id=\"documenttrans6\">6</span></a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data editorial-footnote\" isnote=\"Y\"><p class=\"bottom_0\">See <a href=\"/paper-summary/revelation-1-august-1831-dc-58\" class=\"referenceInPop\" pop=\"/ajax/papers/tooltip/revelation-1-august-1831-dc-58\" poptitle=\"Revelation, 1 August 1831 [D&amp;C\n58]\">Revelation, 1 Aug. 1831</a> [D&amp;C 58:4].</p><hr></div></div></aside> <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>by this and also others, and also one received of <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>late, I know that Zion, in the own due time of the <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>Lord will be redeemed,<aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"1707857970039343109\"><a href=\"#1707857970039343109\" class=\"editorial-note-static staticPopup\" title=\"Note\" name=\"trans7\"><span id=\"documenttrans7\">7</span></a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data editorial-footnote\" isnote=\"Y\"><p class=\"bottom_0\">See <a href=\"/paper-summary/revelation-12-october-1833-dc-100\" class=\"referenceInPop\" pop=\"/ajax/papers/tooltip/revelation-12-october-1833-dc-100\" poptitle=\"Revelation, 12\nOctober 1833 [D&amp;C 100]\">Revelation, 12 Oct. 1833</a> [D&amp;C 100:13].</p><hr></div></div></aside> but how many will be <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>the days of her purification, tribulation and <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>affliction, the Lord has kept hid from my eyes; <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>and when I enquire concerning this subject the <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>voice of the Lord is, Be still, and know that I am <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>God!<aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"5801292855943699060\"><a href=\"#5801292855943699060\" class=\"editorial-note-static staticPopup\" title=\"Note\" name=\"trans8\"><span id=\"documenttrans8\">8</span></a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data editorial-footnote\" isnote=\"Y\"><p class=\"bottom_0\">See Psalm 46:10. Six days after he wrote this letter, JS dictated a <a href=\"/paper-summary/revelation-16-17-december-1833-dc-101\" class=\"referenceInPop\" pop=\"/ajax/papers/tooltip/revelation-16-17-december-1833-dc-101\" poptitle=\"Revelation, 16–17 December 1833 [D&amp;C\n101]\">revelation</a> reiterating this sentiment. (<a href=\"/paper-summary/revelation-16-17-december-1833-dc-101\" class=\"referenceInPop\" pop=\"/ajax/papers/tooltip/revelation-16-17-december-1833-dc-101\" poptitle=\"Revelation, 16–17 December 1833 [D&amp;C\n101]\">Revelation, 16–17 Dec. 1833</a> [D&amp;C 101:16].)</p><hr></div></div></aside> all those who suffer for my name shall <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>reign with me,<aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"2499679906337235322\"><a href=\"#2499679906337235322\" class=\"editorial-note-static staticPopup\" title=\"Note\" name=\"trans9\"><span id=\"documenttrans9\">9</span></a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data editorial-footnote\" isnote=\"Y\"><p class=\"bottom_0\">See 2 Timothy 2:12.</p><hr></div></div></aside> and he that layeth down his <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>life for my sake shall find it again.<aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"11271268584875720303\"><a href=\"#11271268584875720303\" class=\"editorial-note-static staticPopup\" title=\"Note\" name=\"trans10\"><span id=\"documenttrans10\">10</span></a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data editorial-footnote\" isnote=\"Y\"><p class=\"bottom_0\">See Luke 9:24; and <a href=\"/paper-summary/revelation-6-august-1833-dc-98\" class=\"referenceInPop\" pop=\"/ajax/papers/tooltip/revelation-6-august-1833-dc-98\" poptitle=\"Revelation,\n6 August 1833 [D&amp;C\n98]\">Revelation, 6 Aug. 1833</a> [D&amp;C 98:13].</p><hr></div></div></aside> Now <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>there are two things of which I am ignorant and <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>the Lord will not show me— perhaps for a wise <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>purpose in himself. I mean in some respects, <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>and they are these, Why God hath suffered so <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>great calamity to come upon Zion; or what <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>the great moving cause of this great affliction <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>is.<aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"2731789410492172136\"><a href=\"#2731789410492172136\" class=\"editorial-note-static staticPopup\" title=\"Note\" name=\"trans11\"><span id=\"documenttrans11\">11</span></a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data editorial-footnote\" isnote=\"Y\"><p class=\"bottom_0\">JS dictated a <a href=\"/paper-summary/revelation-16-17-december-1833-dc-101\" class=\"referenceInPop\" pop=\"/ajax/papers/tooltip/revelation-16-17-december-1833-dc-101\" poptitle=\"Revelation, 16–17 December 1833 [D&amp;C\n101]\">revelation</a> about a week later that read, “There were jar[r]ings and contentions envyings and strifes and lustful and covetous desires among them . . . they were slow to hearken unto the voice of the Lord their God Therefore the Lord their God is slow to hearken unto their prayers to answer them in the day of their trouble In the day of their peace they esteemed lightly my council.” (<a href=\"/paper-summary/revelation-16-17-december-1833-dc-101\" class=\"referenceInPop\" pop=\"/ajax/papers/tooltip/revelation-16-17-december-1833-dc-101\" poptitle=\"Revelation, 16–17 December 1833 [D&amp;C\n101]\">Revelation, 16–17 Dec. 1833</a> [D&amp;C 101:6–8].)</p><hr></div></div></aside> <span class=\"deleted\">These two things</span> and again by what means <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>he will return her back to her <aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"3058497487981269285\"><a href=\"#3058497487981269285\" class=\"reference staticPopup\" ro=\"x6228\" topic=\"x6228\" title=\"Inheritance\">inheritance</a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data\" isnote=\"Y\" isnonsearchable=\"Y\"><input type=\"hidden\" value=\"Inheritance\"><p>Generally referred to land promised by or received from God for the church and its members. A January 1831 revelation promised church members a land of inheritance. In March and May 1831, JS dictated revelations commanding members “to purchase lands for an...</p><a class=\"more\" href=\"/topic/inheritance\">View Glossary</a></div></div></aside> <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>with songs of everlasting Joy upon her head.<aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"18172826648852358239\"><a href=\"#18172826648852358239\" class=\"editorial-note-static staticPopup\" title=\"Note\" name=\"trans12\"><span id=\"documenttrans12\">12</span></a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data editorial-footnote\" isnote=\"Y\"><p class=\"bottom_0\">See Isaiah 35:10; 51:11; <a href=\"/paper-summary/revelation-circa-7-march-1831-dc-45\" class=\"referenceInPop\" pop=\"/ajax/papers/tooltip/revelation-circa-7-march-1831-dc-45\" poptitle=\"Revelation, circa 7 March 1831 [D&amp;C\n45]\">Revelation, ca. 7 Mar. 1831</a> [D&amp;C 45:71]; and <a href=\"/paper-summary/revelation-29-october-1831-dc-66\" class=\"referenceInPop\" pop=\"/ajax/papers/tooltip/revelation-29-october-1831-dc-66\" poptitle=\"Revelation, 29\nOctober 1831 [D&amp;C 66]\">Revelation, 29 Oct. 1831</a> [D&amp;C 66:11].</p><hr></div></div></aside> <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>These two things brethren, are in part kept back <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>that they are not plainly &lt;​shewn unto me. but there are some things that are plainly​&gt; manifest, that has <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>incured &lt;​th[e]​&gt; displeasure of <span class=\"deleted\">displeasure</span> the Almighty. <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>when I contemplate upon all things that have been [p. 71]</div></body></html>", "calendarsOfDocuments": [], "versions": [{"versionTitle": "Letter to Edward Partridge and Others, 10 December 1833", "versionLink": "/paper-summary/letter-to-edward-partridge-and-others-10-december-1833/1", "versionFeatured": "true"}, {"versionTitle": "Letterbook 1", "versionLink": "/paper-summary/letterbook-1/82", "versionFeatured": ""}, {"versionTitle": "History, 1838–1856, volume A-1 [23 December 1805–30 August 1834]", "versionLink": "/paper-summary/history-1838-1856-volume-a-1-23-december-1805-30-august-1834/398", "versionFeatured": ""}, {"versionTitle": "“History of Joseph Smith”", "versionLink": "/paper-summary/history-of-joseph-smith/213", "versionFeatured": ""}], "images": {"smallImageUrl": "/7633/7633_ms155_2_01_lb1_071_thumb.jpg", "mediumImageUrl": "/7633/7633_ms155_2_01_lb1_071_med.jpg", "largeImageUrl": "/7633/7633_ms155_2_01_lb1_071.jpg", "downloadImageUrl": "/7633/7633_ms155_2_01_lb1_071_download.jpg"}, "imageCredit": "", "facsimile": "", "dzUrlXml": "/7633/7633_ms155_2_01_lb1_071.xml", "classification": "Documents", "publishedStatus": "FinalContent", "accessionNumber": "192", "requestedPageNumber": "2", "numberOfPages": "6", "editorialTitle": "Letter to Edward Partridge and Others, 10 December 1833", "cleanEditorialTitle": "Letter to Edward Partridge and Others, 10 December 1833", "date": "December 10, 1833", "handwriting": "No handwriting information was found.", "footnotes": [{"id": "244866308034964329", "text": "<html><head></head><body><p class=\"bottom_0\">See Ezekiel 20:40; and Isaiah 57:13; see also <a href=\"/paper-summary/revelation-22-23-september-1832-dc-84\" class=\"referenceInPop\" pop=\"/ajax/papers/tooltip/revelation-22-23-september-1832-dc-84\" poptitle=\"Revelation, 22–23 September 1832\n[D&amp;C 84]\">Revelation, 22–23 Sept. 1832</a> [D&amp;C 84:2].</p></body></html>", "number": 4, "type": "number", "toenote": "", "longcitation": null}, {"id": "4040432009142619244", "text": "<html><head></head><body><p class=\"bottom_0\">Four months earlier, on 2 August 1833, JS dictated a <a href=\"/paper-summary/revelation-2-august-1833-a-dc-97\" class=\"referenceInPop\" pop=\"/ajax/papers/tooltip/revelation-2-august-1833-a-dc-97\" poptitle=\"Revelation,\n2 August 1833–A [D&amp;C\n97]\">revelation</a> that warned if <a href=\"/topic/zion\" class=\"referenceInPop\">Zion</a> “observe not to do whatsoeve[r] I have <a href=\"/topic/commandment\" class=\"referenceInPop\">commanded</a> her I will visit her according to all her works with sore afflictions.” (<a href=\"/paper-summary/revelation-2-august-1833-a-dc-97\" class=\"referenceInPop\" pop=\"/ajax/papers/tooltip/revelation-2-august-1833-a-dc-97\" poptitle=\"Revelation,\n2 August 1833–A [D&amp;C\n97]\">Revelation, 2 Aug. 1833–A</a> [D&amp;C 97:26].)</p></body></html>", "number": 5, "type": "number", "toenote": "", "longcitation": null}, {"id": "10413754604294689899", "text": "<html><head></head><body><p class=\"bottom_0\">See <a href=\"/paper-summary/revelation-1-august-1831-dc-58\" class=\"referenceInPop\" pop=\"/ajax/papers/tooltip/revelation-1-august-1831-dc-58\" poptitle=\"Revelation, 1 August 1831 [D&amp;C\n58]\">Revelation, 1 Aug. 1831</a> [D&amp;C 58:4].</p></body></html>", "number": 6, "type": "number", "toenote": "", "longcitation": null}, {"id": "1707857970039343109", "text": "<html><head></head><body><p class=\"bottom_0\">See <a href=\"/paper-summary/revelation-12-october-1833-dc-100\" class=\"referenceInPop\" pop=\"/ajax/papers/tooltip/revelation-12-october-1833-dc-100\" poptitle=\"Revelation, 12\nOctober 1833 [D&amp;C 100]\">Revelation, 12 Oct. 1833</a> [D&amp;C 100:13].</p></body></html>", "number": 7, "type": "number", "toenote": "", "longcitation": null}, {"id": "5801292855943699060", "text": "<html><head></head><body><p class=\"bottom_0\">See Psalm 46:10. Six days after he wrote this letter, JS dictated a <a href=\"/paper-summary/revelation-16-17-december-1833-dc-101\" class=\"referenceInPop\" pop=\"/ajax/papers/tooltip/revelation-16-17-december-1833-dc-101\" poptitle=\"Revelation, 16–17 December 1833 [D&amp;C\n101]\">revelation</a> reiterating this sentiment. (<a href=\"/paper-summary/revelation-16-17-december-1833-dc-101\" class=\"referenceInPop\" pop=\"/ajax/papers/tooltip/revelation-16-17-december-1833-dc-101\" poptitle=\"Revelation, 16–17 December 1833 [D&amp;C\n101]\">Revelation, 16–17 Dec. 1833</a> [D&amp;C 101:16].)</p></body></html>", "number": 8, "type": "number", "toenote": "", "longcitation": null}, {"id": "2499679906337235322", "text": "<html><head></head><body><p class=\"bottom_0\">See 2 Timothy 2:12.</p></body></html>", "number": 9, "type": "number", "toenote": "", "longcitation": null}, {"id": "11271268584875720303", "text": "<html><head></head><body><p class=\"bottom_0\">See Luke 9:24; and <a href=\"/paper-summary/revelation-6-august-1833-dc-98\" class=\"referenceInPop\" pop=\"/ajax/papers/tooltip/revelation-6-august-1833-dc-98\" poptitle=\"Revelation,\n6 August 1833 [D&amp;C\n98]\">Revelation, 6 Aug. 1833</a> [D&amp;C 98:13].</p></body></html>", "number": 10, "type": "number", "toenote": "", "longcitation": null}, {"id": "2731789410492172136", "text": "<html><head></head><body><p class=\"bottom_0\">JS dictated a <a href=\"/paper-summary/revelation-16-17-december-1833-dc-101\" class=\"referenceInPop\" pop=\"/ajax/papers/tooltip/revelation-16-17-december-1833-dc-101\" poptitle=\"Revelation, 16–17 December 1833 [D&amp;C\n101]\">revelation</a> about a week later that read, “There were jar[r]ings and contentions envyings and strifes and lustful and covetous desires among them . . . they were slow to hearken unto the voice of the Lord their God Therefore the Lord their God is slow to hearken unto their prayers to answer them in the day of their trouble In the day of their peace they esteemed lightly my council.” (<a href=\"/paper-summary/revelation-16-17-december-1833-dc-101\" class=\"referenceInPop\" pop=\"/ajax/papers/tooltip/revelation-16-17-december-1833-dc-101\" poptitle=\"Revelation, 16–17 December 1833 [D&amp;C\n101]\">Revelation, 16–17 Dec. 1833</a> [D&amp;C 101:6–8].)</p></body></html>", "number": 11, "type": "number", "toenote": "", "longcitation": null}, {"id": "18172826648852358239", "text": "<html><head></head><body><p class=\"bottom_0\">See Isaiah 35:10; 51:11; <a href=\"/paper-summary/revelation-circa-7-march-1831-dc-45\" class=\"referenceInPop\" pop=\"/ajax/papers/tooltip/revelation-circa-7-march-1831-dc-45\" poptitle=\"Revelation, circa 7 March 1831 [D&amp;C\n45]\">Revelation, ca. 7 Mar. 1831</a> [D&amp;C 45:71]; and <a href=\"/paper-summary/revelation-29-october-1831-dc-66\" class=\"referenceInPop\" pop=\"/ajax/papers/tooltip/revelation-29-october-1831-dc-66\" poptitle=\"Revelation, 29\nOctober 1831 [D&amp;C 66]\">Revelation, 29 Oct. 1831</a> [D&amp;C 66:11].</p></body></html>", "number": 12, "type": "number", "toenote": "", "longcitation": null}], "meta": {"/paper-summary-PageTitle": "Letter to Edward Partridge and Others, 10 December 1833, Page 71", "/paper-summary-MetaTitle": "Letter to Edward Partridge and Others, 10 December 1833, Page 71", "/paper-summary-MetaDescription": "with their blood.4See Ezekiel 20:40; and Isaiah 57:13; see also Revelation, 22–23 Sept. 1832 [D&C 84...", "/paper-summary-MetaUrl": "/paper-summary/letter-to-edward-partridge-and-others-10-december-1833/2", "/paper-summary-MetaImage": "/bc-jsp/content/jsp/images/7633/7633_ms155_2_01_lb1_071_thumb.jpg"}, "scribes": [{"id": "per63", "name": "Frederick G. Williams"}], "printVolumeLocation": "<a href=\"http://www.josephsmithpapers.org/articles/documents-volume-3-february-1833-march-1834\" class=\"externalLink\" xmlns:srchdoc=\"https://ldsc.xmlref.com/local/ldschurch/searchDocuments\" xmlns:lds=\"https://ldsc.xmlref.com/local/ldschurch\"><span class=\"title\">JSP,</span> D3:375–381</a>"}, "legal": {}, "disableVerticalScroll": true, "documentURI": "/published/jsp/searchable/papers/30495/30495-0002.xml", "searchOptions": [{"name": "| This Document", "value": "